## Steps

### STEP 1 -- Configure the DUT as an NTP client, with a reachable and an UNREACHABLE server

Both configured in one go, deliberately, so that the exchange under test and the control that
must not match are **in the same capture, at the same instant, through the same interface**:

```
awplus(config)#ntp server 10.38.22.33          ! the testbox's own ntpd -- must be used
awplus(config)#ntp server 10.38.22.40          ! an unused address on vlan10 -- must NOT be
awplus#show running-config | include ntp
ntp server 10.38.22.40
ntp server 10.38.22.33
```
(Note the stored order is the reverse of the entry order.) 10.38.22.40 is inside vlan10's
`10.38.22.32/27` and nothing is there -- the box's own ARP table reads it `FAILED`.

Capture over the whole leg:
```
tools/tb capture tb277 ntp1021 eth3 240 t33400-s1-sync.pcap udp port 123 or arp host 10.38.22.40
```

**STEP 1 PASS.**

